{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1430549-vohzd-war-ghoul-in-requiem","id":1430549,"title":"Vohzd (War Ghoul) in Requiem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-31T03:01:19-08:00","id":1430549,"title":"Vohzd (War Ghoul) in Requiem","content":"Does exist statistics and mechanics for this creature translated for Requiem? How would you stat them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T03:45:09-08:00","id":1430550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1430549-vohzd-war-ghoul-in-requiem#post1430549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does exist statistics and mechanics for this creature translated for Requiem? How would you stat them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean a vohzd crafted using an homebrew 2ed vicissitude bloodline discipline?<br /> Or a sort of blood magic construct (in this case in secrets of the covenant it is listed a similar ritual) ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T03:59:24-08:00","id":1430552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1430549-vohzd-war-ghoul-in-requiem?p=1430550#post1430550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean a vohzd crafted using an homebrew 2ed vicissitude bloodline discipline?<br /> Or a sort of blood magic construct (in this case in secrets of the covenant it is listed a similar ritual) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The former. Let's say the translation of a Tzimisce war Ghoul <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T04:42:13-08:00","id":1430557,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Vohzd</b><br /> <br /> I wrote up an version a while ago using the Horror rules from the Chronicles of Darkness corebook. I figured it was easier to strip the concept down to its core (a horrible flesh-crafted monstrosity) then getting caught up in disciplines and blood magic. In this write up I left the back story open enough for a ST to fill in the blanks. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Vohzd</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The exact origin of the creature called the \u201cVozhd\u201d is unknown. It was recovered from an abandoned laboratory by a team of agents working for the Cheiron Group (the second such team, the Vozhd destroyed the first). The creature is a mind numbingly awful, multi-limbed hulk of flesh \u2013 seemingly comprised of multiple human and animal bodies fused together and weighing nearly 2 tons. The word \u201cVozhd\u201d was taken from a nameplate outside of the shattered cell where the creature made its lair. While not mindless, it lashes out violently at the least provocation (unless heavily sedated, at which point it exhibits a degree of human intelligence). The creature currently resides under heavy sedation at an undisclosed location. All other information recovered from the laboratory has been classified.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Determined; Vice: Violent<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Crush, Kill, Destroy<br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 1, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 8, Dexterity 4, Stamina 8<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 1, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Athletics 3, Brawl 3, Intimidate 6, Survival 3<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Demolisher, Indomitable, Iron Skin 2 (Advanced, Epic), Striking Looks 2 (Nightmarish)<br /> <b>Potency:</b> 4<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 11<br /> <b>Size:</b> 13<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 2<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 18 (Species Factor 6)<br /> <b>Health:</b> 21<br /> <b>Weapons/Attacks</b><br /> Bite [+0L melee; 11 dice]<br /> Smash &amp;Trample [+1L melee; 11 dice]<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Hideous Strength*, Madness &amp; Terror, Many Limbed*, Mass Slam*, Regenerate<br /> <br /> <b>Hideous Strength:</b> The creature\u2019s might is truly formidable; by spending a point of Willpower, the Horror can increase its Strength by its Potency until the end of the scene. Furthermore, it adds its Potency as automatic successes on Strength + Stamina rolls made to perform a feat of strength, such as lifting a massive object or breaking free of restraints.<br /> <br /> <b>Many-Limbed:</b> The Creature has a collection of additional limbs, which could be additional arms, legs, tentacles or stranger appendages. These limbs fail and strike at any nearby target. As long as the horror has it Defense available and is not Dodging, any character coming into the monsters reach takes one point of bashing damage. This damage continues once per turn as long as the enemy stays within range, and occurs on the enemy\u2019s turn. If the creature spends a point of Willpower, this damage becomes one lethal until its next turn.<br /> <br /> <b>Mass Slam:</b> The horror is adept at using its monstrous bulk to crash into groups of smaller adversaries. The creature may inflict Smash &amp;Trample attacks upon multiple adjacent targets with a combined Size 13. Roll its dice pool separately for each target, but count it as only one attack.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","